# agw-test-env: template for this host's real values

Copy this file to `inventory.local.md` in this same directory, then fill in your host's real
values in place of every placeholder below. The copy is auto-ignored by the repo's `*.local.*`
gitignore rule (this `.example` file is the committed template; `inventory.local.md` itself
never is), so your real values stay local to this machine.

This file fills in the generic, committed `agw-test-env` skill's operator-parameter
placeholders. Never put a real value in THIS file (the `.example` is committed); only in your
own `inventory.local.md` copy.

## Parameter values

| Placeholder | Value | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `<aws-account-id>` | `<your-aws-account-id>` | Account hosting the aws-ec2 vm-site. |
| `<iam-user>` | `<your-iam-user>` | Dedicated least-privilege EC2+SSM IAM user. |
| `<aws-region>` | `<your-aws-region>` | The AWS region the aws-ec2 site is pinned to. |
| `<azure-subscription>` | `<your-azure-subscription>` | Subscription used for azure-vm testing. |
| `<azure-resource-group>` | `<your-azure-resource-group>` | The Azure resource group VMs are created in. Note any host-sharing caution that applies to it. |
| `<azure-region>` | `<your-azure-region>` | Region used for VM creation (quota). |
| `<azure-rg-region>` | `<your-azure-rg-region>` | Region the resource group itself lives in (can differ from the VM's). |
| `<remote-lima-host>` | `<your-remote-lima-host>` | The remote machine running Lima for the remote vm-site, if you have one. |
| `<vm-host-alias>` | `<your-vm-host-alias>` | vm-site name / ssh-alias root for `<remote-lima-host>`. |
| `<remote-user>` | `<your-remote-user>` | ssh/lima user on `<remote-lima-host>`. |
| `<host-owner>` | `<your-host-owner>` | Who else, if anyone, shares the host (only relevant on a shared machine). |
| `<system-slug>` | `<your-system-slug>` | The agentworks system slug seeded on this host (prefixes VM/tailnet names). |

## Notes specific to this host

Add anything a reader would need that is not captured by the table above: known standing
gotchas, account-activation quirks, host-sharing cautions, or anything else specific to your
environment that the generic skill cannot know in advance.

Record which agentworks checkout the `agw` on this host is installed editable from, by path.
The skill says `agw` runs whatever branch that checkout has out, so the path is what tells a
reader which code a run actually drove.

If you run local lima, this is where its install lives: the `uv` binary path, the path of the
checkout agw runs from there, and the exact method for refreshing that checkout to the branch
under test (the skill says the refresh is mandatory before every local-lima run; only you know
how it is done here).
